at elaine  says you know that translational  component  of come to me with your problem that  your business problem  and i'm going to tell you if it's a data  problem or if it's not a data problem at  all  and how data science you know can or  can't be used to solve it  is report the best output in terms of  the solution that we're going to deliver  to you or do we need to  build you a model and put that in an api  that  fits into our current business process  um so that somebody's not you know  running a model on their own laptop so i  think  it really comes down to problem solving  at a high level  and i think that a lot of the sales and  marketing material that's  that's been out there for a while  doesn't do us justice  as the data scientists who are on the  ground trying to communicate and trying  to help  the business move forward and solve its  problems  thank you mike and um if you wouldn't  mind introducing yourself i think  it'd be helpful to maybe share your your  company too  oh sure you don't want me to just rant  the whole time  no i love that i appreciate it yeah  my name is michael thomas i'm the chief  data scientist at catch brook analytics  which we're a data science consulting  firm out of the hartford connecticut  area  really focusing on that whole end-to-end  data science  life cycle in terms of getting the  problem the business problem  translating it into a data problem and  then um  actually deploying the solution kind of  from end to end  and we highly specialize in our i'm a  certified our studio  and shiny instructors so live breathe  r when i can  thanks mike it's it does seem like a lot  of  the topics end up going back to  communication  and elaine i was just curious like what  are  specific things that you think data  scientists can do  today or like things that you've maybe  taught to people on your team  to really get better at communicating  data science  one of the things i know i've told  people on my team  repeatedly over time 